### Right Panel

```astro
---
// src/components/layout/Right.astro
import Chat from '../chat/Chat';

interface Props {
  chatConfig?: any;
}

const { chatConfig } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="right-panel-container">
  {chatConfig ? (
    <Chat config={chatConfig} client:load />
  ) : (
    <div class="content-section">
      <!-- Default content when chat is not enabled -->
      <slot />
    </div>
  )}
</div>

<style>
  .right-panel-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: var(--panel-bg);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  
  .content-section {
    flex: 1;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding: 1rem;
  }
</style>
```

## CSS Layout

The main layout container should use CSS Grid for flexible panel arrangement:

```css
.layout-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "left top top top right"
    "left center center center right"
    "left center center center right"
    "left bottom bottom bottom right";
  grid-template-columns: auto 1fr 1fr 1fr auto;
  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr 1fr auto;
  height: 100vh;
  width: 100vw;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.left-panel {
  grid-area: left;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.top-panel {
  grid-area: top;
}

.center-panel {
  grid-area: center;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.bottom-panel {
  grid-area: bottom;
}

.right-panel {
  grid-area: right;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

/* Panel width variations */
.left-panel.quarter, .right-panel.quarter {
  width: 25vw;
}

.left-panel.half, .right-panel.half {
  width: 50vw;
}

.left-panel.full, .right-panel.full {
  width: 100vw;
}

/* Responsive adjustments */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .layout-container {
    grid-template-areas:
      "top top top top top"
      "center center center center center"
      "center center center center center"
      "bottom bottom bottom bottom bottom";
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;
  }
  
  .left-panel, .right-panel {
    position: fixed;
    height: 100vh;
    z-index: 100;
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }
  
  .right-panel {
    right: 0;
    transform: translateX(100%);
  }
  
  .left-panel.active {
    transform: translateX(0);
  }
  
  .right-panel.active {
    transform: translateX(0);
  }
}
```

## Panel Visibility Controls

Implement controls to toggle panel visibility:

```astro
---
// Example of panel toggle buttons
---

<button id="toggle-left" aria-label="Toggle left panel">
  <Icon name="menu" />
</button>

<button id="toggle-right" aria-label="Toggle right panel">
  <Icon name="chat" />
</button>

<script>
  document.getElementById('toggle-left').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const leftPanel = document.querySelector('.left-panel');
    leftPanel.classList.toggle('active');
  });
  
  document.getElementById('toggle-right').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const rightPanel = document.querySelector('.right-panel');
    rightPanel.classList.toggle('active');
  });
</script>
```

## Panel Resize Functionality

For resizable panels, implement resize handles:

```astro
<div class="resize-handle left-resize"></div>
<div class="resize-handle right-resize"></div>

<style>
  .resize-handle {
    position: absolute;
    width: 5px;
    height: 100%;
    cursor: col-resize;
    z-index: 10;
  }
  
  .left-resize {
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
  }
  
  .right-resize {
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Implement resize functionality using JavaScript
  // This is a simplified example
  const leftResize = document.querySelector('.left-resize');
  const leftPanel = document.querySelector('.left-panel');
  
  leftResize.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    document.addEventListener('mousemove', resizeLeft);
    document.addEventListener('mouseup', stopResize);
  });
  
  function resizeLeft(e) {
    leftPanel.style.width = e.clientX + 'px';
  }
  
  function stopResize() {
    document.removeEventListener('mousemove', resizeLeft);
    document.removeEventListener('mouseup', stopResize);
  }
</script>
```

## Best Practices

1. **Accessibility**:
   - Ensure all panels are keyboard navigable
   - Use proper ARIA attributes for dynamic content
   - Maintain sufficient color contrast

2. **Performance**:
   - Use client directives judiciously
   - Implement lazy loading for panel content
   - Optimize CSS for minimal repaints

3. **Responsive Design**:
   - Design for mobile-first
   - Implement collapsible panels for small screens
   - Use appropriate breakpoints

4. **State Management**:
   - Store panel visibility state in URL or localStorage
   - Implement smooth transitions between states
   - Preserve user preferences

5. **Theming**:
   - Use CSS variables for consistent styling
   - Support both light and dark modes
   - Maintain consistent visual hierarchy

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

- **DON'T** hardcode dimensions; use relative units
- **DON'T** nest panels too deeply
- **DON'T** use fixed positioning without considering overflow
- **DON'T** forget to handle touch events for mobile
- **DON'T** implement complex animations that might cause performance issues 